<title>POLAND: Poland raises minimum five-yr bond price to 80.55.</title>
<headline>Poland raises minimum five-yr bond price to 80.55.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland raised the minimum five-year fixed bond price to 80.55 from 80.47 at the last auction on February 20, the National Bank of Poland said.</p>
<p>It said the average accepted price also rose to 80.75 from 80.72.</p>
<p>The treasury sold 200 million zlotys worth of the bonds, due June 12, 2001, the amount on offer, after investors bid for 280 million.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 653 9700</p>
